// "ExchangeControl" = exchange control of two permanents
// ([CR#701.12a..701.12b]): each player simultaneously gains control of the
// permanent the other controlled. The body is the `Simultaneous` batch primitive — the
// exchange works BECAUSE both halves read ONE pre-application snapshot
// (each `ControllerOf` evaluates before either half applies), land as one
// batch of `ControlChanged` facts, and are all-or-nothing ([CR#701.12a]:
// if the entire exchange can't be completed, no part occurs; a
// same-controller exchange does nothing, [CR#701.12b]).
//
// Usage: ExchangeControl(a, b) — e.g. ExchangeControl(Target(0), Target(1)).
//
// `Simultaneous`/`GainControl` are restricted to THIS macro family's bodies
// until the engine's batch wiring generalizes.
(
    name: "ExchangeControl",
    template: "exchange control of ${0} and ${1}",
    kinds: [Effect],
    params: [Reference, Reference],
    body: Simultaneous([
        GainControl(Param(0), ControllerOf(Param(1))),
        GainControl(Param(1), ControllerOf(Param(0))),
    ]),
)
